Acceptance criteria:
  No diagnostic/raw-face pixels appear in clean preview, output window, virtual camera or exported video.
  Camera indexing/backends and locked/live/checked states are visually understandable.
  Blink tests cover the reported 0.51/0.66 closed-eye scenario through explicit calibration,
  actual renderer output and transient blink responsiveness, not just classifier constants.
  Lossless export preserves processed frame pixels, dimensions, source timing and compatible audio;
  unsupported HDR/rotation/format cases fail explicitly, never silently convert quality.
  Output is written safely without overwriting input/existing files, with progress and cooperative cancel.
  Existing CLI behavior and privacy fail-closed boundaries remain intact.
  User screenshots/raw imagery stay private; no automatic live capture or remote publication.

Completion evidence:
